WEBVTT

00:13.480 --> 00:16.310
[NARRATOR] The walls
stood for a century.

00:16.340 --> 00:19.980
A bastion of peace and security.

00:22.020 --> 00:25.550
Gone was the terror
of living at their mercy.

00:25.590 --> 00:29.990
Mankind had acclimated
to living like cattle.

00:32.430 --> 00:33.760
Then...

00:33.800 --> 00:38.770
[Intense music plays]

00:47.640 --> 00:49.010
[NARRATOR] The Titans
breached what we'd

00:49.040 --> 00:51.080
long taken for granted.

00:51.110 --> 00:54.310
The fight for humanity's
survival began.

00:57.120 --> 00:58.650
Death reigned,

00:58.690 --> 01:01.620
claiming soldiers
and civilians alike.

01:01.690 --> 01:04.490
The casualties were staggering.

01:04.490 --> 01:07.130
Staggering, too,
was the hard-won knowledge

01:07.160 --> 01:10.130
that Titans were
hiding among our own.

01:10.170 --> 01:12.530
Five years after
the first wall fell,

01:12.570 --> 01:14.500
we successfully
captured one of these

01:14.540 --> 01:17.240
treacherous creatures alive.

01:17.270 --> 01:21.270
A fellow soldier.
Annie Leonhart.

01:31.150 --> 01:34.190
[NARRATOR]
And yet,

01:34.220 --> 01:37.190
even as the smoke
of battle cleared,

01:37.230 --> 01:41.230
the next threat
was already close at hand.

01:52.170 --> 01:54.110
[SOLDIERS gasp]

01:54.140 --> 01:55.110
What the--?

01:55.140 --> 01:56.080
Guys! Look!

01:56.110 --> 01:58.410
[MALE SOLDIER 26A]
Wh-What is that?

02:02.650 --> 02:04.380
[MALE SOLDIER 26B]
It's a Titan!

02:04.420 --> 02:06.320
[MALE SOLDIER 26C gasps]
In the wall?

02:06.350 --> 02:08.050
[MALE SOLDIER 26D]
Impossible!

02:08.090 --> 02:10.420
[HANGE and MOBLIT gasp]

02:10.460 --> 02:12.490
Section Commander,
your orders?

02:12.530 --> 02:16.630
Uh. Well, I'm not sure.

02:16.670 --> 02:20.700
[HANGE] Is, is this just
a coincidence, or...?

02:20.740 --> 02:23.800
Oh, no.
Surely it doesn't mean!

02:23.840 --> 02:25.310
[Gasps]

02:25.370 --> 02:28.810
[Panting]

02:28.840 --> 02:30.710
[HANGE]
Pastor Nick?

02:30.750 --> 02:33.550
[NICK]
Listen to me.

02:33.580 --> 02:37.820
Whatever else you do,
don't let sunlight touch it!

02:39.420 --> 02:40.720
Mm.

02:47.500 --> 02:51.160
[Opening theme song,
sung in Japanese]

04:18.650 --> 04:19.690
[MALE SOLDIER 26E]
For the time being,

04:19.720 --> 04:21.690
we've covered the
Wall Titan with sheets.

04:21.720 --> 04:23.390
It seems to be holding up.

04:23.430 --> 04:25.960
Further measures will be taken
after sundown, commander.

04:25.990 --> 04:27.790
Understood.

04:27.830 --> 04:28.900
[MALE SOLDIER 26E]
Forgive me, sir,

04:28.930 --> 04:31.230
but what are we supposed
to make of all this?

04:31.270 --> 04:32.600
I mean, I never imagined
there could be

04:32.630 --> 04:34.430
Titans inside the walls.

04:34.470 --> 04:37.270
[ERWIN]
Why would you? No one did.

04:37.310 --> 04:38.770
There are only those who knew

04:38.810 --> 04:41.540
and those of us
completely in the dark.

04:43.810 --> 04:45.980
Why are they
keeping quiet about this?

04:46.010 --> 04:48.610
It's an earth-shattering
discovery for god's sake.

04:48.650 --> 04:50.980
What's the point
of playing it off?

04:51.020 --> 04:52.990
Status quo, right?

04:53.020 --> 04:56.490
Yeah, higher ups
play it close to the vest.

04:56.520 --> 04:59.030
All this carnage,
and they couldn't even

04:59.060 --> 05:02.330
be bothered to come up
with a decent cover story.

05:05.370 --> 05:07.600
[HANGE]
All right.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.440
You wanna tell me
what's going on?

05:10.470 --> 05:11.740
[MOBLIT grunts]

05:11.770 --> 05:15.810
[HANGE] Why a Titan?
What's the purpose?

05:15.840 --> 05:17.440
What on Earth's
the point of having one

05:17.480 --> 05:21.250
hidden inside the wall?

05:21.280 --> 05:23.850
And why choose
to keep it a secret?

05:23.890 --> 05:28.220
I need answers, and I'm gonna
need them right now.

05:31.490 --> 05:32.890
[NICK sighs]

05:32.930 --> 05:34.760
I don't have time
for this nonsense.

05:34.800 --> 05:37.530
I'm a busy man. My flock
has been devastated!

05:37.570 --> 05:41.700
I demand restitution!
Do you know who I am?

05:41.740 --> 05:44.570
Let me down
from here this instant!

05:44.610 --> 05:46.470
If that's what you want.

05:46.510 --> 05:47.970
[Groans]

05:48.010 --> 05:50.440
[HANGE] Will straight
down do the trick?

05:50.480 --> 05:52.450
[NICK cries out]

05:52.480 --> 05:54.750
--Commander!
--Hold!

05:54.780 --> 05:56.780
Let me ask you something.

05:56.820 --> 05:59.050
Do you have any concept
of how many Scouts

05:59.090 --> 06:02.560
have laid down their lives
fighting these monsters?

06:02.590 --> 06:04.620
More than you can count!

06:04.660 --> 06:07.530
They died fighting
for your freedom!

06:07.560 --> 06:09.030
I was with them!

06:09.060 --> 06:12.900
I was willing to
lay down my own life!

06:12.930 --> 06:15.970
Now, you can explain,
or you take the plunge.

06:16.000 --> 06:21.610
Your choice. I can always
move on to the next blowhard.

06:21.640 --> 06:23.880
Matter of fact,
they'd probably know

06:23.910 --> 06:26.950
more than you anyway.
Why am I bothering?

06:26.980 --> 06:30.280
Let go! Unhand me!

06:30.320 --> 06:32.550
[HANGE] That's kind of
what I had in mind.

06:32.590 --> 06:34.020
Do it!

06:34.060 --> 06:35.990
Don't try to call my bluff.

06:36.020 --> 06:37.460
Please, don't!

06:37.490 --> 06:40.690
You think I'm afraid to die
in the service of my belief?

06:40.730 --> 06:43.860
We fulfill our duty
whatever the cost!

06:44.870 --> 06:47.870
I don't care!
The Lord is my shepherd!

06:47.900 --> 06:52.610
Let his humble servant fall!

06:55.680 --> 07:00.110
Lord, grant release.

07:02.880 --> 07:05.820
--[HANGE grunts]
--[NICK groans]

07:06.960 --> 07:08.550
[HANGE chuckles]

07:08.590 --> 07:11.660
Lighten up.
I was just kidding around.

07:11.690 --> 07:13.790
[Breathe quaveringly]

07:13.830 --> 07:18.060
[HANGE] Come on,
Pastor Nick. Spill it.

07:18.100 --> 07:19.970
Are all the walls
made of Titans?

07:20.000 --> 07:22.500
At least tell me that much.

07:23.810 --> 07:25.810
Section Commander.

07:25.840 --> 07:30.710
[HANGE] Ugh. How long's it been
since I felt like this?

07:30.750 --> 07:33.410
Wow. Must've been
when I stepped outside

07:33.450 --> 07:35.980
the walls for the first time.

07:39.490 --> 07:42.660
Talk about terrifying.

07:42.690 --> 07:45.490
[Bell rings]

07:45.530 --> 07:46.990
[Gasps]

07:48.730 --> 07:51.530
[TOMAS] Hurry! I have
to tell Commander Erwin!

07:51.570 --> 07:53.170
Hyah!

07:53.200 --> 07:55.900
The Titans have
breached Wall Rose!

07:55.940 --> 07:59.870
[Bell continues ringing]

08:16.460 --> 08:17.760
[CHRISTA] How much
longer do you think

08:17.790 --> 08:19.930
--they'll keep us here?
--[YMIR] Who knows.

08:19.960 --> 08:21.060
Y'know, my village
happens to be

08:21.100 --> 08:23.700
just a little bit south
of where we are now.

08:23.730 --> 08:27.000
Huh. Town where I'm from's
pretty close by, too.

08:27.040 --> 08:28.570
[CONNY sighs]

08:28.600 --> 08:32.440
Why can't I
go see my people?

08:32.470 --> 08:34.770
Maybe I'll just
sneak out after dark.

08:34.810 --> 08:36.880
My people told me not to
bother coming back home

08:36.910 --> 08:39.780
till I'm normal, so...
there's that.

08:39.810 --> 08:42.480
Hm. Well, folks where I grew
up always tried to tell me

08:42.520 --> 08:45.020
I was too puny to be a soldier.

08:45.050 --> 08:47.720
No question I had
the brains for it.

08:47.760 --> 08:50.490
I was top ten
in my class, actually.

08:50.530 --> 08:52.020
Somebody's gonna
be eatin' their words,

08:52.060 --> 08:53.790
that's a promise.

08:53.830 --> 08:57.760
Conny, I'll help you
if you really wanna go.

08:57.800 --> 09:00.030
Yeah? Why would you?

09:00.070 --> 09:02.640
Doesn't this
feel a bit strange?

09:02.670 --> 09:04.700
We're on standby
in our plain clothes.

09:04.740 --> 09:06.510
They won't let us
wear our uniforms.

09:06.570 --> 09:09.180
We can't even train.

09:09.210 --> 09:11.540
What's even more suspicious:

09:11.580 --> 09:13.780
our superiors
are armed to the teeth.

09:13.820 --> 09:16.880
We're inside the wall,
not at the front line.

09:16.920 --> 09:19.420
So who exactly
are we fighting?

09:19.450 --> 09:21.490
[Sighs]
I don't know, man.

09:21.520 --> 09:23.560
Maybe they're
worried about bears.

09:23.590 --> 09:25.760
Sure. Bears.

09:25.790 --> 09:28.130
[REINER] All you need
for bears are guns.

09:29.600 --> 09:31.530
[SASHA groans]

09:36.500 --> 09:39.000
[Gasps]

09:39.040 --> 09:42.170
Uh. Guys, I think I'm
hearing footsteps!

09:42.210 --> 09:43.510
What?

09:43.580 --> 09:45.510
Knock if off, Sasha.

09:45.550 --> 09:48.650
So what, you're trying
to tell us Titans are here?

09:48.680 --> 09:50.180
Come on, that would
only be possible

09:50.220 --> 09:52.050
if Wall Rose had fallen.

09:52.090 --> 09:54.520
[MICHE inhales sharply]

09:54.560 --> 09:56.660
What is it, Miche?

09:56.690 --> 10:00.890
Tomas. Ride out of here.
Take three couriers.

10:00.930 --> 10:01.930
[Gasps]

10:01.960 --> 10:04.860
Notify the districts.

10:04.900 --> 10:06.830
[MICHE] The odds of there
being any Titans hiding

10:06.870 --> 10:09.940
in the hundred and forth
Cadet Corp are low.

10:11.210 --> 10:14.240
We've got multiple Titans
incoming from the south!

10:14.280 --> 10:18.080
Wall Rose has been compromised!

10:19.580 --> 10:22.950
Look, I'm not pulling
your leg! I hear something!

10:22.980 --> 10:24.120
[Window squeaks]

10:24.150 --> 10:25.620
[NANABA]
Is everyone here?

10:25.690 --> 10:27.190
What it is, Nanaba?

10:27.220 --> 10:28.290
We've got company.

10:28.320 --> 10:31.090
Approximately 500 meters
to the south and closing.

10:31.130 --> 10:32.960
Titans. Headed this way.

10:32.990 --> 10:35.630
There's no time to suit up
with your ODM gear.

10:35.660 --> 10:37.300
I want everyone on a horse STAT.

10:37.330 --> 10:40.930
Evacuate every home and
settlement in the area.

10:40.970 --> 10:42.230
Get to it.

10:42.270 --> 10:44.300
The south? But that's--

10:44.340 --> 10:45.970
[Gasps]

10:46.010 --> 10:48.670
Do we know if the wall's
really been breached?

10:50.340 --> 10:52.610
[NANABA] Ride! I'm sorry,
but I'm afraid lunch

10:52.650 --> 10:54.650
is going to have to wait!

10:59.750 --> 11:01.250
Miche.

11:02.990 --> 11:06.130
[MICHE] Nine of them.
In that swarm up ahead.

11:10.130 --> 11:12.730
[NANABA] They must've
broken through Wall Rose.

11:16.800 --> 11:19.310
[NANABA] Damn it.
We never even got the chance

11:19.340 --> 11:22.940
to figure out what in
god's name these things are.

11:22.980 --> 11:26.350
Now, it's too late.

11:26.380 --> 11:30.650
Humanity has lost.
This is the end.

11:32.290 --> 11:35.390
Like hell it is.
We're not done.

11:36.990 --> 11:40.760
Not yet. A person only
loses when they give in.

11:40.800 --> 11:42.330
Remember that.

11:43.360 --> 11:45.430
As long as we keep
putting up a fight,

11:45.470 --> 11:47.730
we haven't been beaten!

11:53.440 --> 11:56.680
[MICHE] The second the Titans
reach the woods, we'll split up.

11:56.710 --> 11:58.410
I want four separate teams.

11:58.450 --> 12:01.110
Recruits and soldiers
alike in each unit.

12:01.150 --> 12:02.350
When I give the signal,

12:02.380 --> 12:06.220
we'll scatter in different
directions simultaneously.

12:06.250 --> 12:08.020
Get the word out
to civilians.

12:08.060 --> 12:10.160
Do not engage the enemy!

12:10.190 --> 12:12.930
Which one of you is most
familiar with the area?

12:12.960 --> 12:14.130
Uh, me!

12:14.160 --> 12:16.260
Sir, my home town's
just to the north of here!

12:16.300 --> 12:19.130
I know this region
like the back of my hand!

12:19.170 --> 12:22.900
Conny, too! Go on, tell him!

12:22.940 --> 12:24.340
What's wrong?

12:24.370 --> 12:26.370
My village.

12:26.410 --> 12:28.970
My village is to the south.

12:29.010 --> 12:32.340
That's where the Titans
are coming from.

12:32.380 --> 12:34.880
I can lead you
to nearby settlements,

12:34.920 --> 12:36.880
but afterwards...

12:36.920 --> 12:39.020
...let me go home. Please.

12:40.960 --> 12:42.190
Very well.

12:42.220 --> 12:44.820
Guide the southern team,
then go to your village.

12:44.860 --> 12:45.960
Yes, sir!

12:46.030 --> 12:48.190
I'll come with you.

12:48.230 --> 12:50.730
What? No, you're crazy.

12:50.770 --> 12:52.130
They'll be everywhere.

12:52.170 --> 12:53.500
You think I care?

12:53.530 --> 12:56.300
I was gonna help you
get home anyway, wasn't I?

12:56.340 --> 12:59.440
What about you? You coming?

13:01.410 --> 13:04.880
Of course. Wouldn't
miss it for the world.

13:07.880 --> 13:09.110
[NANABA]
As you have guessed,

13:09.180 --> 13:12.790
today marks the darkest hour
in humanity's history!

13:12.820 --> 13:15.220
Look sharp. If ever
we needed to give our all,

13:15.260 --> 13:18.390
that time is now!
Don't lose heart!

13:18.430 --> 13:19.490
[GELGAR]
They've reached the woods!

13:19.530 --> 13:21.860
The enemy is on top of us!

13:26.500 --> 13:28.130
[MICHE]
Scatter, now!

13:28.170 --> 13:31.240
Ride for everything
you're worth!

13:42.780 --> 13:45.350
[MICHE] No. They're
coming at us full tilt!

13:45.390 --> 13:47.820
[CONNY]
Huh? Holy shit!

13:49.190 --> 13:51.890
[MICHE]
Gelgar!

13:51.930 --> 13:54.330
Take charge
of the southern team!

13:54.360 --> 13:57.130
[GELGAR]
Sir?

13:57.160 --> 13:59.400
Uh, understood.

13:59.430 --> 14:01.830
[FEMALE SOLDIER 26B] Tell me
he's not using himself as bait!

14:01.870 --> 14:03.500
I'll go with him!
I can help!

14:03.540 --> 14:04.800
Stay where you are!

14:04.840 --> 14:07.110
We can't spare
any more soldiers!

14:07.140 --> 14:09.210
Give him some credit.

14:09.240 --> 14:12.310
That man's skills are
second only to Captain Levi.

14:12.350 --> 14:15.550
He'll make it back alive.
Count on it!

14:34.070 --> 14:36.900
[Bellows]

14:54.790 --> 14:59.150
[CARLA] Ugh, Eren.
Another fight? Really?

14:59.190 --> 15:01.820
Yeah, well, I'm not the one
who started it this time!

15:01.860 --> 15:04.030
Those jerks
were making fun of me!

15:04.060 --> 15:09.060
Of course. Did Mikasa
come to your rescue again?

15:09.100 --> 15:10.730
Thank you, dear.

15:15.910 --> 15:18.540
[CARLA] Eren, we don't throw
punches at everyone

15:18.580 --> 15:19.940
who's mean to us.

15:19.980 --> 15:23.980
Being an adult means learning
how to pick your battles.

15:24.010 --> 15:25.850
You want them to think
that you're strong?

15:25.880 --> 15:27.580
Exercise restraint.

15:27.620 --> 15:31.020
Try protecting Mikasa
once in a while.

15:39.460 --> 15:41.830
[EREN groans softly]

16:04.590 --> 16:06.690
[MIKASA exhales]

16:17.800 --> 16:19.530
[MIKASA]
Oh.

16:19.570 --> 16:22.500
It fell. Here.

16:22.540 --> 16:26.170
Get some sleep.
You've gotta be tired.

16:26.210 --> 16:29.510
No. I'm okay.

16:29.550 --> 16:33.510
[EREN] That thing's
seen better days.

16:33.550 --> 16:37.820
I'll grab you a new one if I
can find any with the supplies.

16:38.690 --> 16:40.220
[MIKASA exhales]

16:42.890 --> 16:45.590
--[Door thuds, squeaks]
--[ARMIN] Eren! Mikasa!

16:45.630 --> 16:47.530
They've broken
through Wall Rose!

16:47.560 --> 16:50.030
The Titans! They're coming!

16:56.610 --> 16:57.840
[Door knob clicks]

16:57.870 --> 16:59.710
[LEVI] Ugh. Why can't
the sons of bitches

16:59.740 --> 17:01.810
give us a moment's peace?

17:03.110 --> 17:04.950
[ERWIN]
Can you go?

17:04.980 --> 17:07.020
Like there's a choice.

17:08.050 --> 17:09.920
If I may say so,
sir, very wise

17:09.950 --> 17:12.050
leaving Miche in charge
of the hundred and fourth.

17:12.090 --> 17:15.220
If anyone can handle
the situation, he can.

17:15.260 --> 17:17.990
Yes.

17:18.030 --> 17:19.830
Let's hope so.

17:31.680 --> 17:34.910
[Breathe deeply]

17:36.610 --> 17:38.910
[MICHE]
Only four of them left.

17:44.720 --> 17:47.760
[MICHE]
No. Don't risk it.

17:47.790 --> 17:50.290
I've bought us
more than enough time.

17:52.030 --> 17:54.860
[Wistles]

17:59.040 --> 18:04.070
[MICHE] Still, though.
That Abnormal worries me.

18:04.140 --> 18:05.640
Look at the bastard.

18:05.680 --> 18:10.180
Easily over 17
meters tall. Massive.

18:10.210 --> 18:11.880
And this is the first time
I've ever seen

18:11.920 --> 18:15.850
one of them covered
with, what, fur?

18:15.890 --> 18:17.890
It's just lumbering around.

18:17.920 --> 18:19.920
Why doesn't it try to rush me?

18:19.990 --> 18:22.120
Definitely an Abnormal, but...

18:22.160 --> 18:25.030
--[HORSE 26A neighs]
--[MICHE gasps]

18:25.700 --> 18:27.560
[MICHE]
Ah. There you are.

18:27.600 --> 18:31.770
Looks like I won't have to hold
out for sundown after all.

18:33.200 --> 18:38.040
[HORSE 26A whinnies]

18:38.070 --> 18:40.980
[MICHE] What the--?
It went for the horse?

18:41.980 --> 18:43.950
Aw, come on!

18:46.050 --> 18:48.050
[HORSE 26A whinnies]

18:52.890 --> 18:54.360
[MICHE grunts]

18:54.390 --> 18:56.890
[Groans]

19:00.730 --> 19:04.730
[Yells]

19:04.770 --> 19:06.570
[DEEP VOICE]
Wait.

19:24.120 --> 19:27.360
[MICHE groans]

19:27.420 --> 19:31.760
You must not have heard me.
I told you to wait.

19:31.800 --> 19:34.030
[Squelch]
[MICHE groans]

19:37.800 --> 19:41.740
[Panting]

19:41.770 --> 19:44.040
[Gasps]

19:51.350 --> 19:54.880
May I ask what you call
that strange weapon of yours?

19:54.950 --> 19:58.090
[Gasps]

19:59.490 --> 20:01.160
The thing attached
to your waist

20:01.190 --> 20:03.960
that allows you to fly.

20:03.990 --> 20:13.400
[Gasps and stammers]

20:13.440 --> 20:18.170
Huh. I'm fairly certain
we speak the same language.

20:18.210 --> 20:22.110
Perhaps you're too frightened
to formulate a response?

20:22.150 --> 20:25.450
I notice you also use swords.

20:25.480 --> 20:27.120
Fascinating.

20:27.150 --> 20:29.950
Must mean you know
we reside in the nape.

20:29.990 --> 20:32.020
Ah, well.

20:32.060 --> 20:34.520
Suppose I'll just
take it back with me.

20:34.560 --> 20:37.190
[MICHE screams]

20:41.060 --> 20:43.400
--[Clink]
--[MICHE gasps]

20:54.110 --> 20:58.850
[Breathe heavily]

20:58.880 --> 21:01.780
Not yet. A person only loses
when they give in.

21:01.820 --> 21:04.950
As long as we keep
putting up a fight.

21:08.930 --> 21:12.490
[MICHE] As long as
we keep putting up a fight,

21:12.530 --> 21:16.030
we haven't been beaten!

21:16.070 --> 21:19.230
[Bellows]

21:19.270 --> 21:20.770
[BEAST TITAN]
Huh?

21:20.800 --> 21:24.870
Oh. You can all move now.

21:27.980 --> 21:30.040
[Yells]

21:30.110 --> 21:34.120
No! No!

